{"step_index":1567,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:42:05Z","input_tokens":2279,"cache_read_tokens":76928,"output_tokens":2268,"content":"The **3-Tier Production Invoice Extraction Pipeline** has been implemented, verified, and deployed to the backend and client fallback engine.\n\n---\n\n### Implementation Breakdown\n\n#### Step 1: Table-Anchor Boundary Slicing ([`utils/invoiceTextParser.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/invoiceTextParser.js))\n- **`sliceDocumentZones(lines)`**: Slices OCR document text into three distinct vertical zones:\n  1. **Header Zone (Top to Table Header Start):** Detects table header row requiring $\\ge 2$ keywords (`['description', 'item', 'particulars', 'hsn', 'qty', 'rate', 'amount']`). Strictly extracts Vendor Name, GSTIN, Invoice Number, and Date only. Address lines, phone numbers, and shop details can never be parsed as items.\n  2. **Line Item Zone (Strict Table Boundaries):** Confined between table header and table footer (`['subtotal', 'taxable value', 'total tax', 'cgst', 'sgst', 'igst', 'total in words']`). Only products/services located here are extracted.\n  3. **Summary & Tax Zone (Table End to Bottom):** Extracts Subtotal, CGST, SGST, IGST, Word Total, and Grand Total. Bank accounts, IFSC codes, and terms are isolated here and barred from line items.\n\n#### Step 2: Right-to-Left (RTL) Numeric Column Parser ([`utils/invoiceTextParser.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/invoiceTextParser.js#L178-L324))\n- **`parseLineItemRTL(line, itemId)`**: Scans tokens from right to left to prevent embedded numbers in product descriptions (e.g. `20W`, `2.5 sq mm`, `90m`) from corrupting columns:\n  - **Token 1 (Last Number):** Billed Amount (`total_amount`).\n  - **Token 2 (Second-to-Last Number):** Unit Rate (`unit_rate`).\n  - **Token 3 (Third-to-Last Number):** Quantity (`quantity`).\n  - **Token 4 (Optional Number):** 4–8 digit HSN/SAC code.\n  - **Remainder (Left of Tokens):** Product Description.\n- **Sanitization & Guardrails:**\n  - Treats commas strictly as thousands separators (`2,535.00` $\\rightarrow$ `2535.0`, `1,270.00` $\\rightarrow$ `1270.0`).\n  - Discar\n<truncated 81 bytes>\nm `total_amount` (unless an audit discrepancy or discount applies).\n  - Strips leading S.No prefixes and trailing unit abbreviations (`NOS`, `PCS`, `SET`, `KG`, `BOX`, `|`, `[`).\n\n#### Step 3: Gemini Vision Multimodal Extraction as Primary ([`server.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py))\n- **Primary Pipeline:** Direct visual layout extraction using Gemini 2.5 Flash at `temperature=0.0`. Client-side text parsing is strictly a fallback.\n- **Dual Authentication Support:**\n  - `AQ.` tokens: dispatched with `Authorization: Bearer <key>`.\n  - Standard `AIzaSy` keys: dispatched with `x-goog-api-key: <key>`.\n- **Structured Schema:** Enforces standard numeric fields (`quantity`, `unit_rate`, `total_amount`, `subtotal`, `cgst`, `sgst`, `igst`, `declared_total`) while accepting either string or float payloads via Pydantic [`ExtractedInvoice`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py#L48-L59).\n- **Post-Processing Reconciliation:**\n  - Rejects HSN/tax fragments (such as `774` or `20`) or any total $<50\\%$ of subtotal, recalculating:\n    $$\\text{declared\\_total} = \\text{round}(\\text{subtotal} + \\text{cgst} + \\text{sgst} + \\text{igst}, 2)$$\n  - Synchronizes `declared_total` and `total_declared` across [`server.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py), [`utils/clean_items.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/clean_items.py), and [`utils/aiExtractor.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/aiExtractor.js).\n\n---\n\n### Verification Results\n\n- **Pydantic Validation:** Passed string and numeric payload deserialization.\n- **Reconciliation Engine:** Verified that `774` and `<50%` hallucinations are corrected to ₹4,489.90 / expected total.\n- **Bearer & API Key Dispatch:** Verified that `AQ.` tokens send `Authorization: Bearer` and `AIzaSy` keys send `x-goog-api-key`.\n- **Active Service:** The FastAPI server is running on [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000).","thinking":"The file is not a git repository but resides directly in the workspace. Reviewing modified files to confirm all requirements of the request are met. Examining the `invoiceTextParser.js` utility, specifically the table-anchor boundary slicing for vertical document zoning.\n\n\nInitial parsing focuses on extracting specific invoice data including vendor information, invoice number, and date, using defined keyword guards to prevent header information from being misinterpreted as line items. Strict table boundary parsing is implemented for item extraction, focusing on physical products/services with validated rates and discarding invalid entries, followed by a summary and tax zone extraction.\n\nRight-to-left numeric column parsing in the utility is designed to handle potential issues with descriptions containing numbers, cleaning commas and extracting billed amounts, unit rates, quantities, and optional HSN/SAC codes based on numeric token positions.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":1568,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:47:49Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nFIX GST TAX EXTRACTION IN INVOICE PARSER:\n\n1. STOP CAPTURING ITEM QUANTITY/WATTAGE AS TAX:\n   - Do NOT search for generic two-digit numbers when extracting GST. '20' from '20W' or 'Pack of 20' must never be mapped to tax amounts.\n   - Tax extraction must look strictly for tax lines in the summary zone:\n     * CGST line pattern: /(?:CGST|Central GST)[\\s@%]*([0-9\\.]+)?%?[\\s:]*[₹\\s]*([0-9,]+(?:\\.[0-9]{2})?)/i\n     * SGST line pattern: /(?:SGST|State GST)[\\s@%]*([0-9\\.]+)?%?[\\s:]*[₹\\s]*([0-9,]+(?:\\.[0-9]{2})?)/i\n     * IGST line pattern: /(?:IGST|Integrated GST)[\\s@%]*([0-9\\.]+)?%?[\\s:]*[₹\\s]*([0-9,]+(?:\\.[0-9]{2})?)/i\n\n2. INTRA-STATE vs INTER-STATE AUTO-DETERMINATION:\n   - Compare the first 2 digits of the Supplier GSTIN (06) and Buyer GSTIN (06).\n   - If both state codes match (Intra-State):\n     * Set IGST strictly to 0.\n     * Default tax split to CGST + SGST (e.g. 9% + 9% = 18%, giving ₹990 CGST and ₹990 SGST on ₹11,000).\n   - If state codes differ (Inter-State):\n     * Set CGST = 0, SGST = 0, and IGST = 18% (₹1,980.00).\n\n3. CLICK HANDLER SYNC:\n   Ensure clicking the '[18% (Electrical)]' quick button recalculates CGST/SGST/IGST dynamically based on current Subtotal (11,000) and triggers a re-audit immediately.\n\nonly change the following and correct the gst reading and verification do not change any other backend and frotend things\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-03T01:17:49+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
